<title>USA: Fenton, Mo., $20 mln COPs repriced, yields cut.</title>
<headline>Fenton, Mo., $20 mln COPs repriced, yields cut.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>A.G. Edwards &amp; Sons, Inc. said Monday it repriced Fenton, Mo., $20 million bond deal cutting the yield in the 1998 maturity five basis points to a 3.85 percent.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:  </p>
<p>FENTON, MISSOURI CAPITAL IMPROVEMENT PROJECTS</p>
<p>RE: $19,745,000*</p>
<p>CERTIFICATES OF PARTICIPATION</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD &amp; UNDERWRITTEN THE ISSUE.</p>
<p>SEE REPRICING OF 1998 MATURITY.</p>
<p>NOTE CHANGE IN TAKEDOWNS.</p>
<p>MOODY'S: NAF		   S&amp;P: AAA / A-	    FITCH: NAF</p>
<p>					     (MBIA INSD)</p>
<p>DATED: 07/01/1997	    FIRST COUPON: 03/01/1998</p>
<p>DUE: 09/01</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
<p>09/01/1998		  375M    3.85  %	100.00</p>
<p>09/01/1999		  655M    4.20  %	100.00</p>
<p>09/01/2000		  685M    4.25  %	  4.30</p>
<p>						  (Approx. $ Price 99.848)</p>
<p>09/01/2001		  710M    4.40  %	100.00</p>
